---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & Background"
  description="Senior Frontend Engineer and UI Architect with 15+ years of experience across enterprise web architecture, frontend platforms, and applied AI systems."
  schemaType="person"
  wide
>
  <header class="border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-14 sm:py-20 lg:py-24">
    <div class="site-shell grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-end">
      <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <span class="h-px w-10 bg-[var(--accent)]" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--accent)]">About · Orielsy Diaz</p>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display mt-7 max-w-5xl text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.04] tracking-[-0.045em] text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">
          Frontend engineering, UI architecture, and the application layer of AI.
        </h1>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-4 lg:pb-1">
        <p class="max-w-md text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] sm:text-[15px]">
          Senior Frontend Engineer and UI Architect with 15+ years of experience building scalable web applications, enterprise platforms, and high-profile digital experiences.
        </p>
        <div class="font-editorial-mono mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 border-t border-[var(--border-subtle)] pt-4 text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em]">
          <a href="/research" class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] transition-colors hover:text-[var(--accent)]">Research →</a>
          <a href="/projects" class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] transition-colors hover:text-[var(--text-primary)]">Projects →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="site-shell">
    <section class="grid gap-10 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-14 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <p class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Practice</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-5">
        <p class="font-display max-w-4xl text-2xl font-medium leading-[1.35] tracking-[-0.03em] text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-3xl lg:text-[2rem]">
          My deepest professional background is frontend engineering and UI architecture.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-10 border-y border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <article class="grid gap-4 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-7 sm:grid-cols-[56px_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-7">
            <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] text-[var(--accent)]">01</span>
            <div>
              <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">Frontend systems & enterprise interfaces</h2>
              <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                I build enterprise applications, establish reusable component and frontend patterns, modernize long-lived platforms, and turn complex automation and backend functionality into interfaces people can actually use.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="grid gap-4 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-7 sm:grid-cols-[56px_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-7">
            <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] text-[var(--accent)]">02</span>
            <div>
              <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">Applied AI & context systems</h2>
              <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                More recently, I have designed and built repository-specific coding-agent knowledge systems and prototyped an MCP Apps MVP, while evaluating local-model runtimes such as WebLLM and Ollama. Together, these efforts extend my frontend and UI architecture background into <strong class="font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">applied AI, context engineering, and developer tools</strong>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="grid gap-4 py-7 sm:grid-cols-[56px_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-7">
            <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] text-[var(--accent)]">03</span>
            <div>
              <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">The application layer</h2>
              <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                I'm particularly interested in the application layer of AI: how agents, context, tools, and interfaces come together to create useful products and developer experiences.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-14 sm:py-20">
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="lg:col-span-3">
          <p class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">How I Think</p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-xs text-xs leading-6 text-[var(--text-muted)]">
            Three recurring ideas that shape how I approach interface and systems work.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="lg:col-span-9">
          <ol class="grid gap-px border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--border-subtle)] lg:grid-cols-3">
            <li class="flex min-h-[19rem] flex-col bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 sm:p-7">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
                <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] text-[var(--accent)]">01</span>
                <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[8px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Context</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-0.025em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">The Right Context at the Right Time</h2>
              <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                More information is not automatically better. Whether the consumer is an autonomous coding agent or a person navigating a complex product, I tend to think in terms of filtering and surfacing the information or capability useful at that particular moment rather than presenting everything at once.
              </p>
            </li>

            <li class="flex min-h-[19rem] flex-col bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 sm:p-7">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
                <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] text-[var(--accent)]">02</span>
                <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[8px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Capability</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-0.025em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">AI as a Capability, Not Just a Chatbot</h2>
              <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                Chat is only one narrow modality. Structured extraction, inline classification, semantic filtering, contextual actions, and adaptive guidance can become ordinary capabilities inside interface architecture without forcing users into a conversational text box.
              </p>
            </li>

            <li class="flex min-h-[19rem] flex-col bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 sm:p-7">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
                <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] text-[var(--accent)]">03</span>
                <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[8px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Abstraction</span>
              </div>
              <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-0.025em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">Abstraction Should Remove Complexity, Not Relocate It</h2>
              <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                Some of the most rewarding interface problems involve taking complicated underlying automation, backend mechanics, or technical systems and designing an interaction model that makes the capability substantially easier for a person to understand and control.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-14 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <p class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Background</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-5">
        <p class="max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
          Throughout my career, I have led frontend and UI technical direction, established engineering standards, collaborated closely across design and engineering teams, and remained hands-on in the codebase.
        </p>

        <ol class="mt-9 border-y border-[var(--border-subtle)]">
          <li class="grid gap-4 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-6 sm:grid-cols-[128px_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-8">
            <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-[var(--accent)]">2002 — 2006</span>
            <div>
              <h2 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">U.S. Navy</h2>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                I served four years as a Petty Officer (SH3). While serving, I independently designed and developed my ship's website outside my assigned duties, work that was recognized with a Navy Commendation Medal.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="grid gap-4 py-6 sm:grid-cols-[128px_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-8">
            <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">After service</span>
            <div>
              <h2 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">Computer science & web development</h2>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
                After leaving the Navy, I studied Computer Science at William Paterson University and worked part-time as a web developer before moving into frontend engineering full-time.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-14 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <p class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Outside the Work</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-5">
        <p class="font-display max-w-4xl text-xl leading-[1.5] tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--text-secondary)] sm:text-2xl">
          Outside of software, I'm especially interested in modular synthesis, gaming, and the places where physical and digital interfaces meet.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-muted)]">
          MIDI, control surfaces, signal routing, and interactive systems are areas I find myself naturally drawn toward.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <p class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Connect</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-5">
        <div class="grid gap-px border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--border-subtle)] sm:grid-cols-3">
          <a href="https://github.com/orielsy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="group bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-5 transition-colors hover:bg-[var(--bg-secondary)]">
            <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[8px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Code</span>
            <span class="font-display mt-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 text-base font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
              GitHub @orielsy <span class="text-[var(--accent)] transition-transform group-hover:-translate-y-0.5 group-hover:translate-x-0.5" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </span>
          </a>

          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/orielsy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="group bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-5 transition-colors hover:bg-[var(--bg-secondary)]">
            <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[8px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Professional</span>
            <span class="font-display mt-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 text-base font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
              LinkedIn <span class="text-[var(--accent)] transition-transform group-hover:-translate-y-0.5 group-hover:translate-x-0.5" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </span>
          </a>

          <a href="/rss.xml" class="group bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-5 transition-colors hover:bg-[var(--bg-secondary)]">
            <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[8px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Updates</span>
            <span class="font-display mt-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 text-base font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
              RSS <span class="text-[var(--accent)] transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>